From 48b996e974c9c1a9c0a3de513420fa34c41ad27a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felucca dev <dev@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 14:53:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Eight sequences per track (FELUCCA_PATBANK), SEQ SWITCH,
 CHAIN, song sequences, ARP GEN, strum and PLAY chords

Each track plays one of eight sequences (own steps, LEN, 64 automation records).
SEQ > SEQUENCE (fourth SEQ page; KNOB 1..4 pick, PRESETS chains the selected
sequence); MENU > SYSTEM > SEQ SWITCH NOW / END; chained sequences play one after the
other. SONG: PRESETS picks the sequence a cell plays. Project SAVE/LOAD and the autosave
keep the banks in the flash the user sample slots had. ARP MODE GEN: generative notes of
the track's scale, ARP > GEN page. SCL > CHORD: CHRD STR3 / STR7 (black keys choose a
diatonic chord, white keys strum it) and PLAY (white keys play chords shaped by the black
keys held: qualities, sevenths, 9/11/13, INV, BASS, STRM with a speed, ARP); SAVE >
CHORDS sets what each black key does, six built in packs and four user packs, saved with
the music. Version v1.6.1_sequences. Based on 1.6.1.
